 to all persons, especially the poor and vulnerable, guided by Catholic values and the teachings of the Church."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"vision-box","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"label","children":"Vision"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"To be the leading Catholic hospital in Ghana, recognised for excellence in patient care, community health, and the formation of compassionate health professionals."}]]}]]}],["$","$L2",null,{"delay":140,"direction":"right","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"core-values-heading","children":"Our Core Values"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"about-values-grid","children":[["$","div","Faith",{"className":"value-card","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"icon","children":["$","img",null,{"src":"./icons/faith.png","alt":"Faith"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"title","children":"Faith"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"desc","children":"Rooted in Catholic values, we honour the dignity and sanctity of every human life."}]]}],["$","div","Compassion",{"className":"value-card","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"icon","children":["$","img",null,{"src":"./icons/compassion.png","alt":"Compassion"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"title","children":"Compassion"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"desc","children":"We treat every patient with empathy, kindness, and genuine care — regardless of background."}]]}],["$","div","Excellence",{"className":"value-card","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"icon","children":["$","img",null,{"src":"./icons/excellence.png","alt":"Excellence"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"title","children":"Excellence"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"desc","children":"We hold ourselves to the highest clinical and ethical standards in all we do."}]]}],["$","div","Community",{"className":"value-card","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"icon","children":["$","img",null,{"src":"./icons/community.png","alt":"Community"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"title","children":"Community"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"desc","children":"We are deeply committed to the health and wellbeing of the communities we serve."}]]}]]}]]}]]}]}]}],["$","$L3",null,{}],["$","section",null,{"className":"timeline-section","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"container","children":[["$","$L2",null,{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"section-tag","style":{"justifyContent":"center"},"children":["$","span",null,{"children":"Our Journey"}]}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"section-heading","style":{"marginBottom":"5rem","textAlign":"center"},"children":"A History of Healing"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"timeline-container","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"timeline-spine"}],[["$","$L2","EARLY 1955",{"delay":0,"direction":"left","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"timeline-row","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"timeline-content-left","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"timeline-year","children":"EARLY 1955"}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"timeline-title","children":"Humble Beginnings"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"timeline-desc","children":"The hospital’s origins trace back to early 1955, when a temporary camp was established on the current hospital grounds. This shelter initially served as an isolation facility to care for local victims of a smallpox outbreak."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"timeline-image-wrapper","children":["$","$L4",null,{"src":"/images/milestone/gen_photo.jpg","alt":"Humble Beginnings","fill":true,"style":{"objectFit":"fill"},"sizes":"(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 33vw"}]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"timeline-node-container","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"timeline-node"}]}],["$","div",null,{}]]}]}],["$","$L2","LATE 1955",{"delay":100,"direction":"right","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"timeline-row","children":[["$","div",null,{}],["$","div",null,{"className":"timeline-node-container","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"timeline-node"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"timeline-content-right","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"timeline-year","children":"LATE 1955"}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"timeline-title","children":"A Community Challenge"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"timeline-desc","children":"Later that year, local Mass Education Officer Mr. Dwamena suggested transforming the site into a permanent clinic. The Chief and Elders petitioned the Catholic Bishop of Kumasi, Rt. Rev. Van de Bronk. The Bishop issued a challenge: the hospital and its resident doctor would go to whichever community—Hwidiem or Agroyesum—could first provide decent accommodation for the physician. Under the leadership of Nana Akwasi Nyantakyi, the Hwidiem community rallied together, donating cocoa and maize to fund and secure the site and housing."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"timeline-image-wrapper","children":["$","$L4",null,{"src":"/images/milestone/gen_photo.jpg","alt":"A Community Challenge","fill":true,"style":{"objectFit":"cover"},"sizes":"(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 33vw"}]}]]}]]}]}],["$","$L2","1956",{"delay":200,"direction":"left","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"timeline-row","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"timeline-content-left","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"timeline-year","children":"1956"}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"timeline-title","children":"The First Doctor & Official Opening"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"timeline-desc","children":"On November 28, 1955, Dr. J. A. Vervoorn, a young Dutch physician, arrived in Hwidiem. The smallpox shed was quickly converted into a dispensary, and construction began on a four-room block (the site of the current female ward). The clinic was officially opened on December 3, 1956, and began expanding under the management of dedicated Dutch medical organizations (Memisa)."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"timeline-image-wrapper","children":["$","$L4",null,{"src":"/images/milestone/gen_photo.jpg","alt":"The First Doctor & Official Opening","fill":true,"style":{"objectFit":"fill"},"sizes":"(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 33vw"}]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"timeline-node-container","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"timeline-node"}]}],["$","div",null,{}]]}]}],["$","$L2","1970s-1980s",{"delay":300,"direction":"right","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"timeline-row","children":[["$","div",null,{}],["$","div",null,{"className":"timeline-node-container","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"timeline-node"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"timeline-content-right","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"timeline-year","children":"1970s-1980s"}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"timeline-title","children":"Diocesan Shift & OLA Leadership"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"timeline-desc","children":"As the Catholic Church structure evolved, ownership of the hospital was transferred to the newly erected Sunyani Diocese in 1973. Seeking to strengthen the hospital's administration, the late Most Rev. James Kwadwo Owusu invited the Missionary Sisters of Our Lady of Apostles (OLA) to manage the facility. The OLA Sisters officially took over administration on January 28, 1984, marking a new era of structured growth."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"timeline-image-wrapper","children":["$","$L4",null,{"src":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1505751172876-fa1923c5c528?auto=format&fit=crop&w=600&q=80","alt":"Diocesan Shift & OLA Leadership","fill":true,"style":{"objectFit":"cover"},"sizes":"(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 33vw"}]}]]}]]}]}],["$","$L2","2000s",{"delay":400,"direction":"left","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"timeline-row","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"timeline-content-left","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"timeline-year","children":"2000s"}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"timeline-title","children":"Modern Era & Looking Ahead"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"timeline-desc","children":"Through the decades, the hospital has transformed from a single-room dispensary into a robust medical institution. This growth has been sustained by the dedication of its staff, the Government of Ghana, local benefactors, and international partner agencies. Today, the hospital remains committed to continuous growth and serving the community with faith and excellence."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"timeline-image-wrapper","children":["$","$L4",null,{"src":"/images/milestone/2000s.jpg","alt":"Modern Era & Looking Ahead","fill":true,"style":{"objectFit":"fill"},"sizes":"(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 33vw"}]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"timeline-node-container","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"timeline-node"}]}],["$","div",null,{}]]}]}],["$","$L2","2023",{"delay":500,"direction":"right","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"timeline-row","children":[["$","div",null,{}],["$","div",null,{"className":"timeline-node-container","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"timeline-node"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"timeline-content-right","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"timeline-year","children":"2023"}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"timeline-title","children":"Digital Health Initiative"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"timeline-desc","children":"SECH launched electronic health records and telemedicine pilot programmes."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"timeline-image-wrapper","children":["$","$L4",null,{"src":"/images/milestone/digital.jpg","alt":"Digital Health Initiative","fill":true,"style":{"objectFit":"cover"},"sizes":"(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 33vw"}]}]]}]]}]}]]]}]]}]}],["$","section",null,{"id":"team","className":"team-section","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"container","children":[["$","$L2",null,{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"section-tag","children":["$","span",null,{"children":"Our People"}]}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"section-heading","children":"Meet the Team"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"team-custom-grid","children":[["$","$L2","1",{"delay":0,"children":["$","div",null,{"className":"team-card-wrapper","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"team-card-d